      "math_academy_id": "e-2554",
      "problem": "Which of the line segments shown below are congruent?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/fea89643ee848c5cce4ea9844da71fae26f4799c4dbbe5795086a5365fbf3ec9.png)",
      "worked_solution": "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}.$",
